# pilot-ci.yml bless trigger sentinel
#
# Modifying this file in a push to lihaaf-converted causes the bless job
# to run BEFORE benchmark (see .github/workflows/pilot-ci.yml detect-mode).
# This lets us regenerate snapshots after a lihaaf version bump without
# polluting the fork's main branch with a workflow_dispatch trigger.
#
# 2026-05-19 — initial sentinel; bumped install pin to lihaaf 0.1.0-beta.10
#              to exercise #45 framework on this pilot.
# 2026-05-19 — re-trigger bless after fix: top-level fixture_dirs was [],
#              violating spec §3.6 default-suite non-empty rule. Promoted
#              debug_handler group to default; other 4 groups stay as named
#              suites.
# 2026-05-19 — re-trigger bless after fix: features = []. axum-macros is
#              gated behind axum's `macros` feature; without
#              features = ["macros"] in lihaaf metadata, the dylib build
#              doesn't pull axum-macros into deps_dir → fixtures' uses fail.
# 2026-05-19 — re-trigger bless after fix: RUSTFLAGS=-C debug-assertions=on.
#              axum-macros' #[debug_handler] gates its error checks on
#              cfg(debug_assertions); lihaaf hard-codes --release; without
#              this flag the macro is a release-mode no-op and every
#              compile_fail fixture compiles successfully (EXPECTED_FAIL_
#              BUT_PASSED).
# 2026-05-19 — re-trigger bless after fix: per-suite features = ["macros"].
#              lihaaf spec §3.6 says features does NOT inherit from default;
#              named suites that omit it get []. The axum re-export
#              `pub use axum_macros::{debug_handler, debug_middleware}` is
#              gated on the macros feature, so every named suite must
#              explicitly opt in.
# 2026-05-19 — re-trigger bless after fix: per-suite dev_deps. Round 5 left
#              16 fails in from_request + 8 in typed_path on `use serde::*`
#              unresolved despite default-suite dev_deps = ["axum-extra",
#              "serde"]. Explicit per-suite dev_deps to match the project's
#              explicit-config model.
# 2026-05-19 — re-trigger bless after trim: debug_middleware and from_ref
#              don't use serde or axum-extra (per `grep ^use` audit); only
#              from_request + typed_path need dev_deps. Bloat-free per
#              user direction.
